WEBVTT

1
00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.071
Thebes, City of the Living,

2
00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:13.865
crown Jewel of Pharaoh 
SETI the First.

3
00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:21.039
Home of Imhotep, 
Pharaoh's high priest,

4
00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:23.249
keeper of the dead.

5
00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:28.713
Birthplace of Anck-Su-Namun, 
Pharaoh's mistress.

6
00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:31.424
No other man was allowed 
to touch her...

7
00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:58.535
But for their love, they were 
willing to risk life itself.

8
00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.729
To resurrect Anck-Su-Namun,

9
00:03:49.812 --> 00:03:53.942
Imhotep and his priests broke into 
her crypt and stole her body.

10
00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.444
They raced deep into the desert,

11
00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:59.322
taking Anck-Su-Namun's corpse to 
Hamunaptra, City of the Dead,

12
00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.657
HAMUNAPTRA - 1290 B.C.

13
00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.701
ancient burial site for 
the sons of pharaohs

14
00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:06.829
and resting place for 
the wealth of Egypt.

15
00:04:09.832 --> 00:04:14.796
For his love, Imhotep dared the gods' 
anger by going deep into the city,

16
00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:19.175
where he took the black Book of the 
Dead from it's holy resting place.

17
00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:24.347
Anck-Su-Namun's soul had been 
sent to the dark underworld,

18
00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:29.686
her vital organs removed and placed 
in five sacred Canopic jars.

19
00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:02.093
Anck-Su-Namun's soul had 
come back from the dead,

20
00:05:03.386 --> 00:05:06.681
but Pharaoh's bodyguards had 
followed lmhotep and stopped him

21
00:05:06.764 --> 00:05:09.225
before the ritual 
could be completed.

22
00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:27.618
He was to remain sealed 
inside his sarcophagus,

23
00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.246
be undead for all of eternity.

24
00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.791
The Magi would never allow 
him to be released,

25
00:05:33.875 --> 00:05:37.920
for he would arise a walking 
disease, a plague upon mankind,

26
00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:41.340
an unholy flesh-eater with 
the strength of ages,

27
00:05:41.549 --> 00:05:45.762
power over the sands, and 
the Glory of invincibility.

28
00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:22.507
For 3,000 years, men and 
armies fought over this land,

29
00:06:22.632 --> 00:06:25.093
never knowing what 
evil lay beneath it.

30
00:06:41.984 --> 00:06:45.071
And for 3,000 years, 
we, the Magi,

31
00:06:45.154 --> 00:06:48.908
the descendants of Pharaoh's 
sacred bodyguards, kept watch.

32
00:07:03.047 --> 00:07:04.966
You just got promoted.

33
00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.641
Steady!

34
00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.979
- You're with me on this one, right? 
- Your strength gives me strength.

35
00:07:19.647 --> 00:07:20.982
Steady!

36
00:07:24.735 --> 00:07:27.321
Wait! Wait for me!

37
00:07:28.364 --> 00:07:29.907
Steady!

38
00:07:34.996 --> 00:07:36.497
Fire!

39
00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:03.793
Run, Beni! Run!

40
00:09:03.918 --> 00:09:06.754
Get inside! Get inside!

41
00:09:08.506 --> 00:09:11.175
Hey! Don't you close that door!

42
00:09:11.259 --> 00:09:13.302
Don't you close that door!

43
00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:16.991
You will die. You will die.

44
00:11:16.717 --> 00:11:20.179
CAIRO, EGYPT - 3 YEARS LATER

45
00:11:31.649 --> 00:11:33.567
Sacred stones,

46
00:11:34.276 --> 00:11:36.737
sculpture and aesthetics,

47
00:11:37.947 --> 00:11:42.743
Socrates, Seth, volume 
one, volume two,

48
00:11:43.077 --> 00:11:45.121
and volume three.

49
00:11:45.496 --> 00:11:47.248
And...

50
00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:51.460
Tuthmosis. What are 
you doing here?

51
00:11:52.253 --> 00:11:54.004
T. T, t, t...

52
00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:55.631
T.

53
00:11:56.924 --> 00:11:59.593
I'm going to put you 
where you belong!

54
00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:18.028
Help.

55
00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:47.558
Oops.

56
00:12:47.641 --> 00:12:49.768
What... How...

57
00:12:56.025 --> 00:12:58.068
Oh, look at this!

58
00:12:58.736 --> 00:13:00.821
Sons of the pharaohs!

59
00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:04.950
Give me frogs! Flies! Locusts!

60
00:13:05.159 --> 00:13:06.994
Anything but you!

61
00:13:07.828 --> 00:13:10.581
Compared to you, the other 
plagues were a Joy!

62
00:13:10.664 --> 00:13:13.375
I am so very sorry. 
It was an accident.

63
00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:17.755
My girl, when Rameses destroyed 
Syria, that was an accident.

64
00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.549
You are a catastrophe!

65
00:13:20.883 --> 00:13:22.676
Look at my library!

66
00:13:22.843 --> 00:13:24.887
Why do I put up with you?

67
00:13:25.596 --> 00:13:28.432
Well, you put up with 
me because I can...

68
00:13:28.516 --> 00:13:31.310
I can read and write 
Ancient Egyptian,

69
00:13:31.685 --> 00:13:35.105
and I can... I can decipher 
hieroglyphics and hieratic,

70
00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:38.734
and, well, I am the only 
person within 1,000 Miles

71
00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:42.071
who knows how to properly code and 
catalog this library, that's why.

72
00:13:42.154 --> 00:13:45.783
I put up with you because your father 
and mother were our finest patrons.

73
00:13:45.866 --> 00:13:47.243
That's why!

74
00:13:47.535 --> 00:13:49.453
Allah rest their souls.

75
00:13:50.871 --> 00:13:54.542
Now, I don't care how you do it, 
I don't care how long it takes,

76
00:13:54.625 --> 00:13:57.086
straighten up this meshiver!

77
00:14:10.891 --> 00:14:12.101
Hello?

78
00:14:38.168 --> 00:14:39.420
Abdul?

79
00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:42.923
Mohammed?

80
00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.094
Bob?

81
00:15:07.656 --> 00:15:10.492
Have you no respect 
for the dead?

82
00:15:12.411 --> 00:15:16.999
Of course I do. But sometimes 
I'd rather like to join them.

83
00:15:17.082 --> 00:15:21.545
Well, I wish you would do it before you 
ruin my career the way you've ruined yours.

84
00:15:21.629 --> 00:15:24.965
- Now, get out. - My 
dear, sweet baby sister.

85
00:15:25.049 --> 00:15:27.217
I'll have you know

86
00:15:27.301 --> 00:15:30.346
that, at this precise moment, 
my career is on a high note.

87
00:15:30.429 --> 00:15:33.724
High note, ha! Jonathan, please, I'm 
really not in the mood for you.

88
00:15:33.807 --> 00:15:36.226
I've just made a bit of 
a mess in the library,

89
00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.229
and the Bembridge scholars have 
rejected my application form again.

90
00:15:39.313 --> 00:15:42.441
They say I don't have enough 
experience in the field.

91
00:15:47.321 --> 00:15:49.657
You'll always have me, old mum.

92
00:15:52.993 --> 00:15:55.663
Besides, I have just the 
thing to cheer you up.

93
00:15:55.746 --> 00:15:59.166
Oh, no, Jonathan, not 
another worthless trinket.

94
00:15:59.249 --> 00:16:02.252
If I have to take one more piece 
of junk to the curator to try and

95
00:16:02.336 --> 00:16:03.879
sell for you.

96
00:16:07.716 --> 00:16:09.677
Where did you get this?

97
00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.888
On a dig down in Thebes.

98
00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:15.140
My whole life, I've never 
found anything, Evy.

99
00:16:15.182 --> 00:16:17.768
Please tell me I've 
found something.

100
00:16:21.939 --> 00:16:24.316
- Jonathan. 
- Yes?

101
00:16:25.317 --> 00:16:27.403
I think you've found something.

102
00:16:31.532 --> 00:16:32.950
You see the cartouche there?

103
00:16:33.033 --> 00:16:36.537
It's the official Royal seal of 
SETI the First, I'm sure of it.

104
00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.622
- Perhaps. 
- Two questions.

105
00:16:38.706 --> 00:16:41.458
Who the hell was SETI the 
First, and was he rich?

106
00:16:41.542 --> 00:16:43.877
He was the second pharaoh 
of the 19th dynasty,

107
00:16:43.961 --> 00:16:45.754
said to be the wealthiest 
pharaoh of them all.

108
00:16:45.796 --> 00:16:47.297
Good. I like this fellow.

109
00:16:47.381 --> 00:16:49.800
- I like him very much. 
- I've already dated the map.

110
00:16:49.883 --> 00:16:51.427
It's almost 3,000 years old.

111
00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:55.889
And if you look at the hieratic 
just here, well, it's Hamunaptra.

112
00:16:56.223 --> 00:16:58.475
Dear God, don't be ridiculous.

113
00:16:58.892 --> 00:17:01.270
We're scholars, not 
treasure hunters.

114
00:17:01.395 --> 00:17:04.523
Hamunaptra's a myth told by 
ancient Arab storytellers

115
00:17:04.606 --> 00:17:06.191
to amuse Greek and 
Roman tourists.

116
00:17:06.275 --> 00:17:10.654
I know all the blather about the city 
being protected by the curse of a mummy,

117
00:17:10.738 --> 00:17:15.492
but my research has led me to believe that 
the city itself may have actually existed.

118
00:17:15.576 --> 00:17:19.621
- Are we talking about the Hamunaptra? 
- Yes. The City of the Dead.

119
00:17:19.788 --> 00:17:22.958
Where the earliest pharaohs were said 
to have hidden the wealth of Egypt?

120
00:17:23.041 --> 00:17:26.253
Yes, yes, in a big, 
underground treasure chamber.

121
00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:29.256
- Heh! - Oh, come on. 
- Everybody knows the story.

122
00:17:29.339 --> 00:17:32.092
The entire necropolis was rigged to sink 
into the sand on Pharaoh's command?

123
00:17:32.176 --> 00:17:35.179
A flick of a switch, and the whole place 
would disappear beneath the sand dunes,

124
00:17:35.262 --> 00:17:36.513
taking the treasure with it?

125
00:17:36.597 --> 00:17:39.516
As the Americans would say, 
it's all fairy tales and hokum.

126
00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.019
Oh, my goodness! Look at that!

127
00:17:49.234 --> 00:17:52.154
You'be burnt it! You've burned 
off the part with the lost city?

128
00:17:52.321 --> 00:17:54.490
It's for the best, I'm sure.

129
00:17:54.782 --> 00:17:58.827
Many men have wasted their lives in 
the foolish pursuit of Hamunaptra.

130
00:17:58.911 --> 00:18:00.996
No one's ever found it.

131
00:18:01.121 --> 00:18:03.665
Most have never returned.

132
00:18:04.041 --> 00:18:06.627
Come, come! Step 
over the threshold.

133
00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.379
Welcome to Cairo Prison, 
my humble home.

134
00:18:09.463 --> 00:18:12.299
You told me that you got it 
on a dig down in Thebes.

135
00:18:12.382 --> 00:18:14.051
- Yeah, well, I was mistaken. 
- You lied to me.

136
00:18:14.134 --> 00:18:16.386
I lie to everybody. What 
makes you so special?

137
00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.555
- I am your sister. - That 
just makes you more gullible.

138
00:18:18.639 --> 00:18:20.516
You stole it from a drunk 
at the local casbah?

139
00:18:20.599 --> 00:18:23.143
Picked his pocket, actually, so I 
don't think it's a very good...

140
00:18:23.185 --> 00:18:26.313
Stop being so ridiculous. What 
exactly is this man in prison for?

141
00:18:26.396 --> 00:18:28.148
This I did not know.

142
00:18:28.232 --> 00:18:31.026
But when I heard that you were 
coming, I asked him that myself.

143
00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.736
And what did he say?

144
00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:36.281
He said he was just 
looking for a good time.

145
00:18:41.995 --> 00:18:44.581
- This is the man that you 
stole it from? - Yes, exactly?

146
00:18:44.665 --> 00:18:46.792
So why don't we just go sniff 
out a spot of tiff in...

147
00:18:46.834 --> 00:18:48.293
Who are you?

148
00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:51.463
- And who's the broad? 
- "Broad"?

149
00:18:51.547 --> 00:18:55.759
I'm just a local sort of missionary 
chap, spreading the good word,

150
00:18:55.843 --> 00:18:58.720
- but this is my sister, Evy. 
- How do you do?

151
00:18:59.346 --> 00:19:03.058
- Oh, well. Guess she's not a 
total loss. - I beg your pardon?

152
00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:04.935
I'll be back in a moment?

153
00:19:05.018 --> 00:19:08.355
- Ask him about the box. 
- We have found...

154
00:19:08.689 --> 00:19:10.274
Hello. Excuse me?

155
00:19:10.357 --> 00:19:12.985
We both found your puzzle box,

156
00:19:13.443 --> 00:19:15.487
and we've come to 
ask you about it?

157
00:19:16.446 --> 00:19:18.615
- No. 
- No?

158
00:19:18.699 --> 00:19:22.578
No. You came to ask 
me about Hamunaptra.

159
00:19:23.662 --> 00:19:25.998
How do you know the box 
pertains to Hamunaptra?

160
00:19:26.081 --> 00:19:29.543
Because that's where I was 
when I found it. I was there.

161
00:19:30.252 --> 00:19:33.213
But how do we know that's 
not a load of pig's wallow?

162
00:19:33.714 --> 00:19:35.299
- Do I know you? 
- No, no.

163
00:19:35.382 --> 00:19:37.759
I've just got one 
of those faces.

164
00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:45.726
You were actually at Hamunaptra?

165
00:19:47.394 --> 00:19:49.146
- Yeah, I was there. 
- You swear?

166
00:19:49.229 --> 00:19:50.981
- Every damn day. - I 
didn't mean that...

167
00:19:51.064 --> 00:19:55.444
I know. I was there. SETI's 
place. City of the Dead.

168
00:19:56.236 --> 00:19:58.780
Could you tell me 
how to get there?

169
00:20:01.909 --> 00:20:04.369
I mean, the exact location?

170
00:20:04.661 --> 00:20:07.164
- You want to know? 
- Well, yes?

171
00:20:07.247 --> 00:20:09.708
- Do you really want to know? 
- Yes?

172
00:20:13.629 --> 00:20:16.048
Then get me the 
hell out of here!

173
00:20:19.301 --> 00:20:20.761
Do it, lady!

174
00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:27.726
- Where are they taking him? 
- To be hanged?

175
00:20:27.976 --> 00:20:30.854
Apparently, he had 
a very good time?

176
00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.862
I will give you £100 to 
save this man's life.

177
00:20:38.946 --> 00:20:42.366
Madame, I would pay £100 
just to see him hang.

178
00:20:42.449 --> 00:20:44.368
- £200. 
- Proceed!

179
00:20:44.493 --> 00:20:45.619
£300.

180
00:20:47.371 --> 00:20:49.539
Any last requests, pig?

181
00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:52.334
Yeah? Loosen the 
knot and let me go.

182
00:20:56.296 --> 00:20:57.714
Of course we don't let him go!

183
00:21:00.467 --> 00:21:01.760
£500!

184
00:21:03.971 --> 00:21:06.890
And what else? I'm 
a very lonely man.

185
00:21:12.104 --> 00:21:13.188
No!

186
00:21:20.529 --> 00:21:22.489
His neck did not break.

187
00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:28.245
Oh, I'm so sorry. Now, we must 
watch him strangle to death.

188
00:21:37.295 --> 00:21:39.715
He knows the location 
to Hamunaptra.

189
00:21:40.549 --> 00:21:42.718
- You lie. 
- I would never!

190
00:21:42.843 --> 00:21:46.013
Are you telling me this 
filthy, godless son of a pig

191
00:21:46.096 --> 00:21:48.223
- knows where to find the 
City of the Dead? - Yes!

192
00:21:48.307 --> 00:21:49.433
- Truly? 
- Yes!

193
00:21:49.516 --> 00:21:51.852
And if you cut him down, 
we will give you...

194
00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:56.898
- 10 % 
- 50 %

195
00:21:56.982 --> 00:21:58.608
- Twenty. 
- Forty.

196
00:21:58.692 --> 00:22:00.694
- Thirty! 
- Twenty five.

197
00:22:01.069 --> 00:22:02.195
Deal.

198
00:22:04.322 --> 00:22:05.824
Cut him down!

199
00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:19.796
GIZA PORT - CAIRO

200
00:22:21.214 --> 00:22:23.008
Do you really think 
he's going to show up?

201
00:22:23.091 --> 00:22:25.552
Yes, undoubtedly, 
knowing my luck.

202
00:22:26.219 --> 00:22:28.972
He may be a cowboy, but I know 
the breed. His word is his word.

203
00:22:29.056 --> 00:22:33.727
Well, personally I think he's 
filthy, rude, a complete scoundrel.

204
00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:36.313
- I don't like him one bit. 
- Anyone I know?

205
00:22:38.565 --> 00:22:39.649
Oh.

206
00:22:42.235 --> 00:22:43.361
Hello.

207
00:22:43.445 --> 00:22:46.156
Smashing day for the start of 
an adventure, eh, O'Connell?

208
00:22:46.239 --> 00:22:48.241
Yeah. Yeah, smashing.

209
00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:52.162
Oh, no, no, I'd never steal 
from a partner, partner.

210
00:22:53.371 --> 00:22:55.874
That reminds me? No hard 
feelings about the...

211
00:22:55.957 --> 00:22:59.169
- Oh, no, no. Happens all 
the time. - Mr. O'Connell?

212
00:22:59.252 --> 00:23:01.004
Can you look me in the 
eye and guarantee me

213
00:23:01.088 --> 00:23:03.924
this isn't some 
sort of a flimflam?

214
00:23:04.007 --> 00:23:07.386
- Because if it is, I am warning 
you... - You're warning me?

215
00:23:07.636 --> 00:23:09.221
Lady, let me put it this way,

216
00:23:09.304 --> 00:23:11.765
my whole damn Garrison 
believed in this so much

217
00:23:11.848 --> 00:23:14.643
that without orders, they marched 
halfway across Libya and into Egypt

218
00:23:14.726 --> 00:23:15.727
to find that city.

219
00:23:15.811 --> 00:23:19.648
When we got there, all we 
found was sand and blood.

220
00:23:20.857 --> 00:23:22.692
Let me get your bags.

221
00:23:27.614 --> 00:23:29.658
Yes, yes, you're right.

222
00:23:29.783 --> 00:23:33.370
Filthy, rude, a complete scoundrel. 
Nothing to like there at all.

223
00:23:35.372 --> 00:23:37.374
Bright good morning to all.

224
00:23:37.457 --> 00:23:39.709
Oh, no. What are you doing here?

225
00:23:39.793 --> 00:23:43.421
I'm here to protect my 
investment, thank you very much.

226
00:24:05.026 --> 00:24:08.071
Quit playing with your glasses 
and cut the deck, Burns.

227
00:24:08.155 --> 00:24:11.074
Without my glasses I can't see 
the deck to cut it, Dave.

228
00:24:11.158 --> 00:24:13.702
O'Connell, sit down. We 
could use another player.

229
00:24:13.785 --> 00:24:16.830
- I only gamble with my life, 
never my money. - Never?

230
00:24:17.038 --> 00:24:20.667
What if I was to bet you $500 we 
get to Hamunaptra before you?

231
00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:23.837
- You're looking for Hamunaptra? 
- Damn straight we are.

232
00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:26.173
- And who saya we are? 
- He does.

233
00:24:26.673 --> 00:24:29.009
Well... Well, how about it?

234
00:24:29.593 --> 00:24:31.011
Is it a bet?

235
00:24:32.971 --> 00:24:36.558
- All right, you're on. - What 
makes you so confident, Sir?

236
00:24:36.683 --> 00:24:39.895
- What makes you? - We got us a 
man who's actually been there.

237
00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:42.647
Oh, what a coincidence, 
because O'Connell...

238
00:24:43.064 --> 00:24:45.817
Whose play is it? Is it my play? 
I thought...

239
00:24:45.901 --> 00:24:49.321
Gentlemen, we got us a wager. 
Good evening, Jonathan.

240
00:24:49.696 --> 00:24:51.114
Night.

241
00:25:06.421 --> 00:25:08.340
Sorry. Didn't mean to scare you.

242
00:25:08.423 --> 00:25:11.468
The only thing that scares me, 
Mr. O'Connell, are your manners.

243
00:25:12.302 --> 00:25:16.556
- Still angry about that kiss, huh? 
- Well, if you call that a kiss.

244
00:25:22.062 --> 00:25:26.775
Did I miss something? Are we... 
Are we going into battle?

245
00:25:26.858 --> 00:25:29.277
Lady, there's 
something out there.

246
00:25:29.569 --> 00:25:31.321
Something underneath that sand.

247
00:25:31.404 --> 00:25:34.658
Yes, well, I'm hoping to 
find a certain artifact.

248
00:25:34.908 --> 00:25:37.911
A book, actually. My brother 
thinks there's treasure.

249
00:25:38.036 --> 00:25:42.582
- What do you think's out 
there? - In a word? Evil.

250
00:25:42.916 --> 00:25:46.419
The Bedouin and the Tuaregs believe 
that Hamunaptra is cursed.

251
00:25:46.503 --> 00:25:49.756
Oh, look, I don't believe in fairy 
tales and hokum, Mr. O'Connell,

252
00:25:49.839 --> 00:25:53.760
but I do believe one of the most famous 
books in history is buried there.

253
00:25:53.843 --> 00:25:55.303
The Book of Amun-Ra.

254
00:25:55.428 --> 00:25:59.140
It contains within it all the secret 
incantations of the old kingdom.

255
00:25:59.474 --> 00:26:02.060
It's what first interested me 
in Egypt when I was a child.

256
00:26:02.143 --> 00:26:05.605
It's why I came here. 
Sort of a life's pursuit.

257
00:26:05.772 --> 00:26:09.943
And the fact that they say it's made out 
of pure gold makes no never mind to you?

258
00:26:10.485 --> 00:26:12.237
- Right. - You 
know your history.

259
00:26:12.320 --> 00:26:14.114
I know my treasure.

260
00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:20.078
By the way,

261
00:26:20.996 --> 00:26:22.539
why did you kiss me?

262
00:26:22.622 --> 00:26:25.959
I was about to be hanged. It seemed 
like a good idea at the time.

263
00:26:29.629 --> 00:26:32.716
What? What'd I say?

264
00:26:40.015 --> 00:26:42.934
Surprise! My good 
friend, you're alive!

265
00:26:43.018 --> 00:26:47.314
- I was so very, very worried. - Well, 
if it ain't my little buddy, Beni.

266
00:26:48.023 --> 00:26:50.317
- I think I'll kill you. 
- Think of my children.

267
00:26:50.400 --> 00:26:52.319
You don't have any children.

268
00:26:52.402 --> 00:26:54.404
- Someday I might. 
- Shut up!

269
00:26:54.487 --> 00:26:56.823
So, you're the one who's 
leading the Americans?

270
00:26:56.906 --> 00:26:58.867
I might have known. So, 
what's the scam, Beni?

271
00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:02.370
You task them into the middle of the 
desert, and then you leave them to rot?

272
00:27:02.454 --> 00:27:04.164
Unfortunately, no.

273
00:27:04.414 --> 00:27:06.416
These Americans are smart.

274
00:27:06.499 --> 00:27:09.502
They pay me only half now, half 
when I get them back to Cairo.

275
00:27:09.586 --> 00:27:12.839
- So this time I must go all the 
way. - Them's the breaks, huh?

276
00:27:13.923 --> 00:27:16.843
You never believed in 
Hamunaptra, O'Connell.

277
00:27:17.385 --> 00:27:19.304
Why are you going back?

278
00:27:21.222 --> 00:27:24.017
You see that girl? 
She saved my neck.

279
00:27:28.897 --> 00:27:32.275
You always did have 
more balls than brains.

280
00:27:37.197 --> 00:27:39.282
Yeah. Goodbye, Beni.

281
00:27:46.289 --> 00:27:47.666
O'Connell!

282
00:28:00.095 --> 00:28:01.888
George Bembridge...

283
00:28:02.597 --> 00:28:05.016
In 1860...

284
00:28:08.478 --> 00:28:10.688
1865, was...

285
00:28:13.608 --> 00:28:14.776
Was...

286
00:28:14.859 --> 00:28:18.780
Oh, for heaven's sake, girl, it 
wasn't that good of a kiss, anyway.

287
00:28:32.794 --> 00:28:34.754
Where is the map?

288
00:28:35.755 --> 00:28:38.258
It's... It's... There.

289
00:28:38.466 --> 00:28:41.261
And the key? Where is the key?

290
00:28:41.761 --> 00:28:44.347
The key? The key? What key?

291
00:28:44.431 --> 00:28:45.682
Evelyn!

292
00:29:01.573 --> 00:29:03.616
The map! The map! 
I forgot the map!

293
00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:06.995
Relax. I'm the map? 
It's all up here?

294
00:29:07.078 --> 00:29:08.955
Oh, that's comforting.

295
00:29:16.963 --> 00:29:18.631
- The key! 
- Evy.

296
00:29:39.777 --> 00:29:41.404
Hold on to this.

297
00:30:10.183 --> 00:30:11.351
Can you swim?

298
00:30:11.434 --> 00:30:14.103
Of course I can swim, if 
the occasion calls for it.

299
00:30:14.187 --> 00:30:16.439
Trust me. It calls for it.

300
00:30:40.213 --> 00:30:43.299
O'Connell! O'Connell! 
What are we going to do?

301
00:30:43.383 --> 00:30:45.969
- Wait here! I'll go get help! 
- Right!

302
00:31:08.366 --> 00:31:09.909
Americans.

303
00:31:25.091 --> 00:31:27.427
I say, bloody good show, chaps!

304
00:31:28.553 --> 00:31:30.179
And did I panic?

305
00:31:30.388 --> 00:31:32.098
I think not.

306
00:31:44.235 --> 00:31:46.738
Get them out of the water! 
Get them out of the water!

307
00:31:46.821 --> 00:31:49.782
Come on, doggies! Give 
them a smack, would you?

308
00:31:53.369 --> 00:31:55.538
This is a messed-up country.

309
00:31:58.541 --> 00:32:02.503
We've lost everything! All of 
our tools, all the equipment!

310
00:32:02.712 --> 00:32:03.880
All my clothes!

311
00:32:03.963 --> 00:32:05.632
O'Connell!

312
00:32:06.841 --> 00:32:07.967
Hey!

313
00:32:08.468 --> 00:32:10.136
O'Connell!

314
00:32:10.219 --> 00:32:14.182
It looks to me like I've 
got all the horses!

315
00:32:14.641 --> 00:32:16.017
Hey, Beni!

316
00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:20.146
Looks to me like you're on 
the wrong side of the river!

317
00:32:20.313 --> 00:32:21.939
Yeah?

318
00:32:38.998 --> 00:32:41.250
I only want four! Four!

319
00:32:41.334 --> 00:32:43.920
I only want four, not 
a whole bloody herd!

320
00:32:44.003 --> 00:32:47.340
O'Connell! Can you 
believe the cheek?

321
00:32:47.423 --> 00:32:49.258
Just pay the man.

322
00:32:49.342 --> 00:32:51.260
Oh, for heaven's sake.

323
00:32:52.095 --> 00:32:54.389
Can't believe the price 
of these fleabags?

324
00:32:54.472 --> 00:32:57.934
Yes, happy? Very good.

325
00:32:58.017 --> 00:33:00.103
You probably could've 
got them for free.

326
00:33:00.186 --> 00:33:02.980
- All we had to do was give 
him your sister. - Yes.

327
00:33:03.648 --> 00:33:05.775
Awfully tempting, wasn't it?

328
00:33:12.490 --> 00:33:13.741
Awfully.

329
00:33:39.142 --> 00:33:40.810
Never did like camels.

330
00:33:40.893 --> 00:33:44.605
Filthy buggers. They smell, 
they bite, they spit.

331
00:33:45.148 --> 00:33:48.109
- Disgusting. - I think 
they're adorable.

332
00:33:50.403 --> 00:33:51.404
Oh, baby.

333
00:35:40.513 --> 00:35:42.682
This one is strong.

334
00:35:51.524 --> 00:35:53.526
Good morning, my friend.

335
00:36:09.709 --> 00:36:10.793
What the hell we doing?

336
00:36:10.877 --> 00:36:13.754
Patience, my good barat'm. 
Patience.

337
00:36:13.838 --> 00:36:18.551
Remember our bet, O'Connell? First 
one to the city, 500 cash bucks.

338
00:36:18.676 --> 00:36:21.137
A hundred of them bucks is yours 
if you help us win that bet.

339
00:36:21.220 --> 00:36:22.847
Oh, my pleasure.

340
00:36:23.389 --> 00:36:26.559
Hey, O'Connell. Nice camel.

341
00:36:30.980 --> 00:36:32.607
Get ready for it.

342
00:36:33.482 --> 00:36:36.402
- For what? - We're about 
to be shown the way.

343
00:36:50.416 --> 00:36:53.961
- Will you look at that? 
- Can you believe it?

344
00:36:54.295 --> 00:36:55.671
Hamunaptra.

345
00:36:55.755 --> 00:36:57.256
Here we go again.

346
00:37:31.749 --> 00:37:33.292
So long, Beni!

347
00:37:36.420 --> 00:37:38.297
That serves you right.

348
00:38:04.240 --> 00:38:06.534
Go, Evy! Go!

349
00:38:47.700 --> 00:38:49.618
Do they know something we don't?

350
00:38:50.536 --> 00:38:53.789
They are led by a woman. 
What does a woman know?

351
00:38:54.206 --> 00:38:56.250
That's a statue of Anubis.

352
00:38:56.542 --> 00:38:58.169
It's legs go deep underground.

353
00:38:58.252 --> 00:39:02.214
According to Bembridge scholars, that's 
where we'll find a secret compartment

354
00:39:02.298 --> 00:39:04.467
containing the Golden 
Book of Amun-Ra.

355
00:39:07.094 --> 00:39:10.139
Jonathan, you're meant to 
catch the sun with that.

356
00:39:12.058 --> 00:39:15.728
- So, what are these old mirrors 
for? - Ancient mirrors.

357
00:39:16.062 --> 00:39:19.023
It's an ancient Egyptian trick. 
You'll see.

358
00:39:20.232 --> 00:39:22.193
Here, this for you.

359
00:39:24.403 --> 00:39:27.531
Go ahead. It's something I borrowed 
off our American brethren.

360
00:39:27.615 --> 00:39:31.160
I thought you might like it, you 
might need it for when you're...

361
00:39:31.243 --> 00:39:34.497
Yeah? What are you looking at?

362
00:39:44.924 --> 00:39:47.593
Hey, look for bugs. I hate bugs.

363
00:39:48.552 --> 00:39:50.846
Do you realize we're 
standing inside a room

364
00:39:50.930 --> 00:39:53.182
no one has entered 
in over 3,000 years?

365
00:39:54.225 --> 00:39:56.602
What is that God-awful stench?

366
00:40:06.904 --> 00:40:09.990
And then there was light?

367
00:40:11.826 --> 00:40:13.953
Hey, that is a neat trick.

368
00:40:14.286 --> 00:40:16.914
- Oh, my God. It's a 
sah-netjer. - What?

369
00:40:16.997 --> 00:40:19.417
- A preparation room. 
- Preparation for what?

370
00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:21.627
For entering the afterlife.

371
00:40:23.129 --> 00:40:25.881
Mummies, my good son. This is 
where they made the mummies.

372
00:40:49.363 --> 00:40:51.157
The legs of Anubis.

373
00:40:52.283 --> 00:40:56.162
The secret compartment should be 
hidden somewhere inside here.

374
00:41:21.687 --> 00:41:23.856
You scared the bejesus 
out of us, O'Connell.

375
00:41:23.939 --> 00:41:25.232
Likewise.

376
00:41:25.316 --> 00:41:28.486
- Hey, that's my tool Kit. 
- No, I don't think so.

377
00:41:28.569 --> 00:41:31.530
Okay? Perhaps I was mistaken.

378
00:41:32.990 --> 00:41:34.533
Have a nice day, gentlemen.

379
00:41:34.617 --> 00:41:36.577
We have a lot of work to 
be getting along with.

380
00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:39.997
- Push off! This is our dig 
site? - We got here first.

381
00:41:41.999 --> 00:41:44.335
This here's our statue, friend.

382
00:41:44.418 --> 00:41:47.171
I don't see your name 
written on it, pal.

383
00:41:47.463 --> 00:41:50.508
Yes, well, there's 
only four of you

384
00:41:50.841 --> 00:41:52.843
and 15 of me.

385
00:41:53.052 --> 00:41:55.387
Your odds are not so 
great, O'Connell.

386
00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:58.432
- I've had worse. 
- Yeah, me, too.

387
00:42:00.184 --> 00:42:03.646
Oh, look, for goodness' sake, 
let's be nice, children.

388
00:42:04.188 --> 00:42:07.775
If we're going to play together, 
we must learn to share.

389
00:42:09.985 --> 00:42:12.279
There are other places to dig.

390
00:42:16.533 --> 00:42:20.329
According to these hieroglyphics, 
we're underneath the statue.

391
00:42:20.412 --> 00:42:22.206
We should come up right 
between his legs.

392
00:42:22.289 --> 00:42:24.208
When those damn Yanks 
go to sleep...

393
00:42:24.291 --> 00:42:25.834
- No offense. 
- None taken.

394
00:42:25.918 --> 00:42:27.336
We'll dig our way up 
and steal that book

395
00:42:27.419 --> 00:42:28.462
right out from under them?

396
00:42:28.504 --> 00:42:30.881
Are you sure we can find 
this secret compartment?

397
00:42:30.965 --> 00:42:33.842
Oh, yes, if those beastly Americans 
haven't beaten us to it.

398
00:42:33.926 --> 00:42:35.594
- No offense. 
- None taken.

399
00:42:35.678 --> 00:42:37.805
Where'd our smelly 
little friend get to?

400
00:42:46.564 --> 00:42:47.898
Let me get this straight.

401
00:42:47.982 --> 00:42:50.401
They ripped out your guts 
and stuffed them in jars?

402
00:42:50.484 --> 00:42:54.071
They'd take out your heart as well. You 
know how they took out your brains?

403
00:42:54.154 --> 00:42:55.781
I don't think we 
need to know this.

404
00:42:55.864 --> 00:42:59.410
They'd take a sharp, red-hot 
poker, stick it up your nose,

405
00:42:59.493 --> 00:43:03.080
scramble things asbout a bit, and then 
rip it all out through your nostrils.

406
00:43:03.163 --> 00:43:05.499
- That's gotta hurt. - It's 
called mummification.

407
00:43:05.582 --> 00:43:07.668
- You'll be dead when they 
do this. - For the record,

408
00:43:07.751 --> 00:43:10.796
if I don't make it out of here, don't 
put me down for mummification.

409
00:43:10.879 --> 00:43:12.172
Likewise.

410
00:43:21.348 --> 00:43:23.183
Oh, my God. It's a...

411
00:43:24.018 --> 00:43:25.811
It's a sarcophagus.

412
00:43:28.522 --> 00:43:30.858
Buried at the base of Anubis.

413
00:43:32.860 --> 00:43:35.904
He must have been someone 
of great importance.

414
00:43:37.072 --> 00:43:40.034
Or he did something 
very naughty.

415
00:43:42.411 --> 00:43:44.038
Well, who is it?

416
00:43:46.206 --> 00:43:48.667
"He That Shall Not Be Named."

417
00:43:53.339 --> 00:43:55.257
This looks like some 
sort of a lock.

418
00:43:55.341 --> 00:43:57.426
Well, whoever's in here 
sure wasn't getting out.

419
00:43:57.509 --> 00:43:59.136
Yeah, no kidding.

420
00:43:59.219 --> 00:44:02.222
It'd take us a month to crack 
into this thing without a key.

421
00:44:02.306 --> 00:44:03.515
A key?

422
00:44:04.224 --> 00:44:07.269
A key! A key! That's what 
he was talking about!

423
00:44:07.353 --> 00:44:10.022
- Who? 
- The man on the barge,

424
00:44:10.105 --> 00:44:12.024
the one with the hook. He 
was looking for a key.

425
00:44:12.107 --> 00:44:13.776
Hey, that's mine.

426
00:44:18.864 --> 00:44:22.743
Seems that our American friends had a 
little misfortune of their own today.

427
00:44:23.077 --> 00:44:26.622
Three of their 
diggers were melted.

428
00:44:26.830 --> 00:44:28.582
- What? 
- How?

429
00:44:28.791 --> 00:44:30.167
Salt acid.

430
00:44:30.709 --> 00:44:35.255
Pressurized salt acid. Some 
kind of ancient booby trap.

431
00:44:36.173 --> 00:44:38.634
Maybe this place 
really is cursed.

432
00:44:41.970 --> 00:44:44.348
Oh, for goodness' sake, you two!

433
00:44:44.515 --> 00:44:46.725
- You don't believe in curses? 
- No, I don't.

434
00:44:46.809 --> 00:44:50.938
I believe if I can see it and I can touch 
it, it's real. That's what I believe.

435
00:44:51.230 --> 00:44:53.315
I believe in being prepared.

436
00:44:56.151 --> 00:44:58.696
Take this. Stay here.

437
00:44:58.862 --> 00:45:01.657
- No, wait, wait! Wait 
for me. Wait! - Evy!

438
00:45:01.740 --> 00:45:04.910
Excuse me, but didn't the 
man just say stay here?

439
00:45:04.993 --> 00:45:06.036
Evy!

440
00:45:09.123 --> 00:45:12.042
Mr. Henderson! Wake up!

441
00:45:51.707 --> 00:45:53.041
O'Connell!

442
00:46:12.561 --> 00:46:13.562
Enough!

443
00:46:15.272 --> 00:46:18.400
We will shed no more 
blood, but you must leave?

444
00:46:19.234 --> 00:46:21.236
Leave this place or die.

445
00:46:22.279 --> 00:46:23.947
You have one day.

446
00:46:47.721 --> 00:46:48.931
Evelyn.

447
00:46:51.266 --> 00:46:52.351
Hey.

448
00:46:54.228 --> 00:46:57.147
- Are you all right? 
- Yes, I'm fine.

449
00:46:57.940 --> 00:46:59.441
- You sure? 
- Thank you.

450
00:46:59.525 --> 00:47:03.445
That proves it. Old SETI's fortune's 
got to be under this sand.

451
00:47:03.612 --> 00:47:06.615
For them to protect it like this, you 
know there's treasure down there.

452
00:47:06.698 --> 00:47:10.619
No, these men are desert people. 
They value water, not gold.

453
00:47:11.161 --> 00:47:15.249
You know, maybe just at night, 
we could combine forces.

454
00:47:17.709 --> 00:47:19.711
Hey, tough stuff, 
try a right hook.

455
00:47:19.795 --> 00:47:22.339
Ball up your fist and put it... 
Put it up like that.

456
00:47:22.631 --> 00:47:24.383
And then mean it. 
Hit it right here.

457
00:47:24.466 --> 00:47:26.677
- Mean it! 
- Okay.

458
00:47:29.513 --> 00:47:31.974
Okay, it's time for 
another drink.

459
00:47:32.349 --> 00:47:34.643
Unlike my brother, Sir,

460
00:47:35.477 --> 00:47:37.813
I know when to say no.

461
00:47:40.148 --> 00:47:42.401
And unlike your brother, miss,

462
00:47:42.484 --> 00:47:44.361
you, I just don't get.

463
00:47:46.321 --> 00:47:49.199
I know. You're wondering

464
00:47:50.409 --> 00:47:54.496
what is a place like me 
doing in a girl like this.

465
00:47:54.872 --> 00:47:58.792
- Yeah, something like that. 
- Egypt is in my blood.

466
00:47:59.334 --> 00:48:00.586
You see,

467
00:48:00.669 --> 00:48:05.257
my father was a very, 
very famous explorer.

468
00:48:05.591 --> 00:48:07.718
And he loved Egypt so much,

469
00:48:08.010 --> 00:48:11.346
he married my mother, 
who was an Egyptian

470
00:48:11.680 --> 00:48:14.349
and quite an adventurer herself?

471
00:48:15.851 --> 00:48:19.521
I get your father and I 
get your mother, and...

472
00:48:21.231 --> 00:48:23.191
I get him, but...

473
00:48:24.234 --> 00:48:26.236
What are you doing here?

474
00:48:27.613 --> 00:48:31.867
Look, I may not be an explorer

475
00:48:32.284 --> 00:48:36.580
or an adventurer or 
a treasure seeker

476
00:48:36.663 --> 00:48:39.875
or a gunfighter, Mr. O'Connell,

477
00:48:40.584 --> 00:48:45.255
but I am proud of what I am.

478
00:48:46.048 --> 00:48:47.716
And what is that?

479
00:48:47.799 --> 00:48:48.884
I...

480
00:48:51.094 --> 00:48:53.055
am a librarian.

481
00:48:57.225 --> 00:49:00.228
And I am going to kiss you,

482
00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:02.898
- Mr. O'Connell. 
- Call me Rick.

483
00:49:09.446 --> 00:49:10.739
Rick.

484
00:49:47.109 --> 00:49:49.861
- There is a curse upon this 
chest. - Curse, my ass.

485
00:49:49.945 --> 00:49:52.698
- Who cares? - Have a 
care, Mr. Henderson.

486
00:49:52.781 --> 00:49:55.867
In these hallowed grounds, that which 
was set forth in ancient times

487
00:49:55.951 --> 00:49:58.412
- is as strong today as it 
was then. - We understand.

488
00:49:58.495 --> 00:50:00.455
What's it say?

489
00:50:07.629 --> 00:50:10.215
"Death will come on swift wings"

490
00:50:10.298 --> 00:50:13.093
"to whomsoever 
opens this chest."

491
00:50:24.479 --> 00:50:26.398
We should not be here.

492
00:50:27.190 --> 00:50:28.775
This is not good.

493
00:50:28.859 --> 00:50:30.235
It says,

494
00:50:30.318 --> 00:50:32.237
"There is one, the undead,"

495
00:50:32.946 --> 00:50:36.324
"who, if brought back to life, 
is bound by sacred law"

496
00:50:36.408 --> 00:50:38.368
"to consummate this curse."

497
00:50:38.452 --> 00:50:41.288
Let's make sure we don't bring 
anyone back from the dead then.

498
00:50:41.371 --> 00:50:44.332
"He will kill all who 
open this chest"

499
00:50:44.833 --> 00:50:47.586
"and assimilate their 
organs and fluids,"

500
00:50:49.046 --> 00:50:51.590
"and in so doing, 
he will regenerate"

501
00:50:51.923 --> 00:50:54.134
"and no longer be the undead,"

502
00:50:54.676 --> 00:50:57.179
"but a plague upon this Earth."

503
00:50:59.097 --> 00:51:02.267
Well, we didn't come all 
this way for nothing.

504
00:51:02.350 --> 00:51:04.603
- That's right. 
- It's the curse.

505
00:51:04.895 --> 00:51:06.438
It's the curse.

506
00:51:06.521 --> 00:51:10.317
It's the curse! 
Beware of the curse!

507
00:51:10.400 --> 00:51:11.943
Beware!

508
00:51:12.027 --> 00:51:14.780
Stupid superstitious bastard.

509
00:51:17.073 --> 00:51:19.785
Oh, I've dreamt about this 
since I was a little girl.

510
00:51:19.868 --> 00:51:21.286
You dream about dead guys?

511
00:51:21.369 --> 00:51:24.456
Look, the sacred spells 
have been chiseled off.

512
00:51:24.831 --> 00:51:27.959
This man must have been condemned not 
only in this life, but in the next.

513
00:51:28.043 --> 00:51:30.212
- Tough break. - Yeah, 
I'm all tears.

514
00:51:30.295 --> 00:51:33.715
Now, let's see who's 
inside, shall we?

515
00:51:44.309 --> 00:51:46.978
Oh, my God, I hate it when 
these things do that.

516
00:51:47.062 --> 00:51:48.522
Is he supposed to 
look like that?

517
00:51:48.605 --> 00:51:51.024
No, I've never seen a mummy 
look like this before.

518
00:51:51.107 --> 00:51:53.860
He's still... Still...

519
00:51:53.944 --> 00:51:54.986
- Juicy. 
- Juicy.

520
00:51:55.070 --> 00:51:56.321
Yes.

521
00:52:04.704 --> 00:52:06.081
Oh, my God.

522
00:52:06.873 --> 00:52:08.875
It does exist.

523
00:52:08.959 --> 00:52:11.795
- The Book of the Dead. 
- A book?

524
00:52:12.379 --> 00:52:15.006
Who cares about a book? Where 
the hell's the treasure?

525
00:52:15.090 --> 00:52:16.716
This, gentlemen.

526
00:52:17.926 --> 00:52:20.095
This is treasure.

527
00:52:21.555 --> 00:52:24.391
Hell, I wouldn't trade 
you for a brass...

528
00:52:27.102 --> 00:52:29.688
Look at that.

529
00:52:30.063 --> 00:52:32.315
There's your 
treasure, gentlemen.

530
00:52:32.399 --> 00:52:34.401
Now, we're on to something.

531
00:52:50.375 --> 00:52:53.253
I believe you need a 
key to open that book.

532
00:52:55.380 --> 00:52:56.506
Say, O'Connell,

533
00:52:56.590 --> 00:52:59.009
what do you think these 
babies'll fetch back home?

534
00:52:59.092 --> 00:53:03.221
We hear you boys found yourselves a 
nice, gooey mummy. Congratulations.

535
00:53:03.305 --> 00:53:07.642
If you dry that fellow out, you might 
be able to sell him for firewood.

536
00:53:38.465 --> 00:53:40.675
That's called 
stealing, you know?

537
00:53:40.759 --> 00:53:44.512
According to you and my 
brother, it's called borrowing.

538
00:53:47.098 --> 00:53:50.018
I thought the Book of Amun-Ra 
was made out of gold?

539
00:53:50.143 --> 00:53:54.064
It is made out of gold. This 
isn't the Book of Amun-Ra.

540
00:53:54.147 --> 00:53:56.316
This is something else.

541
00:53:56.441 --> 00:53:59.319
I think this may be 
the Book of the Dead.

542
00:53:59.653 --> 00:54:01.363
The Book of the Dead?

543
00:54:01.446 --> 00:54:03.782
Are you sure you're meant to be 
playing around with this thing?

544
00:54:03.865 --> 00:54:05.700
It's just a book.

545
00:54:05.867 --> 00:54:09.621
No harm ever came 
from reading a book.

546
00:54:15.293 --> 00:54:17.712
That happens a lot around here.

547
00:54:20.173 --> 00:54:21.549
So, what's it say?

548
00:54:21.633 --> 00:54:24.761
"Amun Ra. Amun Dei."

549
00:54:25.595 --> 00:54:28.306
It speaks of the night 
and of the day.

550
00:54:42.404 --> 00:54:46.241
No! You must not 
read from the book!

551
00:55:12.851 --> 00:55:14.227
Run!

552
00:55:16.688 --> 00:55:18.356
Go, go!

553
00:55:26.823 --> 00:55:29.034
What have we done?

554
00:55:30.118 --> 00:55:34.039
- Where the hell did they come from? 
- I ain't waiting around to find out.

555
00:55:41.004 --> 00:55:42.380
Oh, Jon!

556
00:55:48.720 --> 00:55:50.138
Scarabs!

557
00:55:50.346 --> 00:55:53.391
Run, Evy! Go, go, go! Run!

558
00:56:09.616 --> 00:56:11.910
I told you to leave or die.

559
00:56:12.285 --> 00:56:13.828
You refused.

560
00:56:14.037 --> 00:56:15.955
Now, you may have killed us all,

561
00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:19.334
for you have unleashed a creasture we 
have feared for more than 3,000 years.

562
00:56:22.962 --> 00:56:26.424
I must now go on the hunt, and 
try and find a way to kill him.

563
00:56:59.207 --> 00:57:02.752
May the good Lord protect 
and watch over me

564
00:57:02.836 --> 00:57:05.338
as a Shepherd watches 
over his flock.

565
00:57:19.185 --> 00:57:21.187
No. Okay.

566
00:57:40.790 --> 00:57:42.125
The language of the slaves...

567
00:57:44.127 --> 00:57:47.130
I may have use for you.

568
00:57:48.756 --> 00:57:50.842
And the rewards...

569
00:57:51.634 --> 00:57:54.304
will be great.

570
00:57:56.014 --> 00:57:57.682
My Prince.

571
00:58:00.477 --> 00:58:04.647
Where are the other 
sacred jars...

572
00:58:26.085 --> 00:58:29.005
I thought you said you didn't believe 
in that fairy tales and hokum stuff.

573
00:58:29.464 --> 00:58:33.843
Having an encounter with a 
3,000-year-old walking, talking corpse

574
00:58:33.927 --> 00:58:35.261
does tend to convert one.

575
00:58:35.345 --> 00:58:38.681
Forget it. We're out the door, 
down the hall, and we're gone.

576
00:58:38.765 --> 00:58:41.851
- Oh, no, we are not. 
- Oh, yes, we are.

577
00:58:41.935 --> 00:58:44.687
Oh, no, we are not. We woke him 
up, and we are going to stop him.

578
00:58:44.771 --> 00:58:46.856
We? What we? We didn't 
read that book.

579
00:58:46.940 --> 00:58:49.609
I told you not to play around with 
that thing. Didn't I tell you?

580
00:58:49.692 --> 00:58:52.862
Yes, right then, me, me, me, me. I, I, I 
woke him up and I intend to stop him.

581
00:58:52.946 --> 00:58:54.364
Yeah? How?

582
00:58:54.447 --> 00:58:57.075
You heard the man. No mortal 
weapons can kill this guy.

583
00:58:57.158 --> 00:59:00.370
Then we are just going to have 
to find some immortal ones.

584
00:59:00.453 --> 00:59:01.913
There goes that we again.

585
00:59:01.996 --> 00:59:04.374
Look, will you listen to me? 
We have to do something.

586
00:59:04.457 --> 00:59:07.085
Once this creature has been reborn, 
his curse is going to spread

587
00:59:07.168 --> 00:59:08.711
until the whole of the 
Earth is destroyed.

588
00:59:08.795 --> 00:59:11.798
- Yeah? Is that my problem? 
- Lt is everybody's problem.

589
00:59:11.881 --> 00:59:14.175
Evelyn, I appreciate you 
saving my life and all,

590
00:59:14.259 --> 00:59:17.553
but when I signed on, I agreed to take 
you out there and to bring you back.

591
00:59:17.637 --> 00:59:20.974
I have done that? End of job. End 
of story. Contract terminated.

592
00:59:21.057 --> 00:59:22.267
That's all I am to you? 
A contract?

593
00:59:22.350 --> 00:59:27.230
You can either tag along with me or you 
can stay here and try and save the world.

594
00:59:27.480 --> 00:59:29.941
- What's it gonna be? 
- I'm staying.

595
00:59:30.024 --> 00:59:33.152
- Fine. 
- Fine.

596
00:59:33.319 --> 00:59:34.529
Fine.

597
00:59:40.702 --> 00:59:44.789
I'm the last of the Royal Air Corps 
still stationed out here, you know...

598
00:59:45.164 --> 00:59:47.875
Some bloody idiot 
spilt his drink.

599
00:59:48.167 --> 00:59:52.130
All the other laddies died in the 
sky and were buried in the sand.

600
00:59:52.213 --> 00:59:54.716
Good chaps, every 
one of them, too.

601
00:59:55.008 --> 00:59:57.635
- Hi, Winston. 
- Yeah...

602
00:59:57.719 --> 01:00:01.389
You know, O'Connell, ever since 
the end of the great war,

603
01:00:01.472 --> 01:00:06.394
there hasn't been a single 
challenge worthy of a man like me.

604
01:00:06.686 --> 01:00:09.147
Yeah? We all got our little 
problems today, Winston.

605
01:00:09.230 --> 01:00:12.692
I just wish I could have 
chucked it in with the others

606
01:00:12.775 --> 01:00:14.944
and gone down in 
flame and Glory,

607
01:00:15.028 --> 01:00:17.447
instead of sitting 
around here, rotting

608
01:00:17.530 --> 01:00:19.115
- of boredom and booze. 
- Of boredom and booze.

609
01:00:19.198 --> 01:00:20.700
Cheers.

610
01:00:23.286 --> 01:00:25.663
Oh, well, back to the airfield.

611
01:00:27.540 --> 01:00:30.126
- Tell me, has your sister always 
been... - Oh, yes, always.

612
01:00:30.209 --> 01:00:33.212
We're all packed up, but the damn boat 
doesn't leave till tomorrow morning.

613
01:00:33.296 --> 01:00:35.632
Tail set firmly between 
your legs, I see.

614
01:00:35.715 --> 01:00:39.177
You can talk. You don't have some 
sacred walking corpse after you.

615
01:00:41.304 --> 01:00:43.056
Sweet Jesus!

616
01:00:43.598 --> 01:00:45.516
Tasted just like...

617
01:00:46.517 --> 01:00:47.894
Blood.

618
01:00:47.977 --> 01:00:53.399
"And the rivers and waters of 
Egypt ran red and were as blood."

619
01:00:55.568 --> 01:00:57.195
He's here.

620
01:01:01.699 --> 01:01:03.618
Oh, looks like it's gonna storm.

621
01:01:03.701 --> 01:01:06.746
- Oh, Evelyn! - Oh, 
so you're still here.

622
01:01:07.580 --> 01:01:09.374
We've got problems.

623
01:01:31.896 --> 01:01:33.147
Hey!

624
01:01:33.898 --> 01:01:36.818
Beni, you little stinkweed. 
Where you been?

625
01:02:02.009 --> 01:02:04.095
We are in serious trouble.

626
01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:23.781
You saved me from the undead.

627
01:02:23.865 --> 01:02:25.032
I thank you.

628
01:02:41.466 --> 01:02:44.802
We are in very serious trouble.

629
01:02:46.637 --> 01:02:48.931
- He does seem to like you Evy. 
- Yeah, what's that about?

630
01:02:48.973 --> 01:02:50.183
What's this guy want?

631
01:02:50.266 --> 01:02:53.352
There's only one person that 
can give us any answers.

632
01:02:53.478 --> 01:02:55.980
- You! 
- Miss Carnahan.

633
01:02:56.522 --> 01:02:59.275
- Gentlemen. - What 
is he doing here?

634
01:02:59.567 --> 01:03:03.237
Do you really want to know, or 
would you prefer to just shoot us?

635
01:03:03.321 --> 01:03:07.325
After what I just saw, I'm willing 
to go on a little faith here.

636
01:03:07.408 --> 01:03:09.994
We are part of an 
ancient secret society.

637
01:03:10.077 --> 01:03:13.789
For over 3,000 yeasrs, we have 
guarded the City of the Dead.

638
01:03:13.873 --> 01:03:18.169
We are sworn at manhood to do any and all 
in our part to stop the High Priest Imhotep

639
01:03:18.252 --> 01:03:19.754
from being reborn 
into this world.

640
01:03:19.837 --> 01:03:21.422
Because of you, we have failed.

641
01:03:21.506 --> 01:03:24.091
You think this justifies the 
killing of innocent people.

642
01:03:24.175 --> 01:03:26.093
To stop this creature? 
Let me think.

643
01:03:26.177 --> 01:03:27.512
- Yes! 
- Yes!

644
01:03:29.138 --> 01:03:31.891
Question. Why doesn't 
he like cats?

645
01:03:31.974 --> 01:03:33.893
Cats are the guardians 
of the underworld.

646
01:03:33.976 --> 01:03:35.853
He will fear them until 
he is fully regenerated?

647
01:03:35.895 --> 01:03:37.146
Then he will fear nothing.

648
01:03:37.230 --> 01:03:39.106
You know how he gets his 
self fully regenerated?

649
01:03:39.190 --> 01:03:43.236
- By killing everyone who opened 
that chest. - And sucking them dry!

650
01:03:43.361 --> 01:03:45.738
Jonathan, will you stop 
playing with that.

651
01:03:45.821 --> 01:03:50.618
When I saw him alive at Hamunaptra, 
he called me Anck-Su-Namun.

652
01:03:52.537 --> 01:03:55.665
And then juat now in Mr. Burns' 
quarters, he tried to kiss me.

653
01:03:55.748 --> 01:03:58.668
It's because of his love for 
Anck-Su-Namun that he was cursed.

654
01:03:58.751 --> 01:04:01.671
- Apparently, even after 3,000 years... 
- He is still in love with her.

655
01:04:01.754 --> 01:04:04.298
Yes, that is very romantic, but 
what has it got to do with me?

656
01:04:04.382 --> 01:04:06.676
Perhaps he will once again try 
to raise her from the dead.

657
01:04:06.717 --> 01:04:07.760
Yes.

658
01:04:07.843 --> 01:04:11.013
And it appears he has already 
chosen his human sacrifice.

659
01:04:13.891 --> 01:04:15.726
Bad luck, old mum.

660
01:04:15.810 --> 01:04:17.478
On the contrary,

661
01:04:17.562 --> 01:04:21.232
it may just give us the time 
we need to kill the creature.

662
01:04:21.315 --> 01:04:23.943
We will need all the 
help we can get.

663
01:04:24.694 --> 01:04:26.612
His powers are growing.

664
01:04:31.409 --> 01:04:35.079
"And he stretched forth his 
hand towards the heavens"

665
01:04:35.162 --> 01:04:39.000
"and there was darkness 
throughout the land of Egypt."

666
01:04:39.875 --> 01:04:41.502
We must stop him 
from regenerating.

667
01:04:41.586 --> 01:04:42.670
Who opened that chest?

668
01:04:42.753 --> 01:04:44.297
There was me and Daniels here.

669
01:04:44.380 --> 01:04:46.716
- And Burns, of course. - And 
that Egyptologist fellow.

670
01:04:46.799 --> 01:04:47.967
What about my buddy, Beni?

671
01:04:48.050 --> 01:04:50.303
No, he scrammed out of there 
before we opened the thing.

672
01:04:50.386 --> 01:04:53.347
- Yeah, he was the smart one. 
- Yeah, that sounds like Beni.

673
01:04:53.431 --> 01:04:56.809
We must find the Egyptologist and bring 
him back to the safety of the fort

674
01:04:56.892 --> 01:04:59.061
- before the creature can 
get to him. - Right.

675
01:04:59.145 --> 01:05:00.730
She stays here. You 
three, come with me.

676
01:05:00.813 --> 01:05:02.690
- Not me... 
- No, no!

677
01:05:02.773 --> 01:05:06.694
Just a minute! You can't leave me 
behind like some old carpetbag.

678
01:05:06.777 --> 01:05:10.114
Who put you in charge, O'Connell? 
What do you think you are doing?

679
01:05:10.197 --> 01:05:11.741
Jonathan! O'Connell!

680
01:05:11.824 --> 01:05:14.619
- Sorry, but he's a bit tall. 
- Jonathan, coward that you are...

681
01:05:14.702 --> 01:05:17.163
O'Connell, you are not 
leaving me in here!

682
01:05:17.705 --> 01:05:20.583
Jonathan, if you don't open 
this door in one minute flat...

683
01:05:20.666 --> 01:05:22.627
- O'Connell... - This 
door doesn't open.

684
01:05:22.710 --> 01:05:24.211
- Let me out of here. 
- She doesn't come out,

685
01:05:24.295 --> 01:05:26.255
- and no one goes in, right? 
- Right.

686
01:05:26.339 --> 01:05:28.007
- Right? 
- Right.

687
01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:30.259
O'Connell! Jonathan!

688
01:05:30.343 --> 01:05:31.594
Let's go, Jonathan?

689
01:05:31.677 --> 01:05:34.805
Oh, I thought I could just astay 
at the fort and reconnoiter.

690
01:05:34.889 --> 01:05:36.182
- Now! 
- Yeah, right.

691
01:05:36.265 --> 01:05:38.726
We're just gonna rescue 
the Egyptologist.

692
01:06:11.509 --> 01:06:15.179
Well, well, well. Let me guess. 
Spring cleaning?

693
01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:20.726
Nice shot.

694
01:06:21.519 --> 01:06:24.689
Oh, Beni, did you fall down? 
Let me help you up.

695
01:06:27.066 --> 01:06:30.653
You came back from the desert with 
a new friend, didn't you, Beni?

696
01:06:30.736 --> 01:06:33.239
What friend? You are 
my only friend.

697
01:06:35.616 --> 01:06:39.453
What the hell are you doing with 
this creep? What's in it for you?

698
01:06:39.537 --> 01:06:43.541
It is better to be the right hand 
of the devil than in his path.

699
01:06:43.624 --> 01:06:46.877
As long as I serve 
him, I am immune.

700
01:06:50.548 --> 01:06:51.966
Immune from what?

701
01:06:53.467 --> 01:06:54.552
What did you say?

702
01:06:54.635 --> 01:06:57.471
I don't wanna tell you. You'll 
just hurt me some more.

703
01:06:57.555 --> 01:07:00.433
What are you looking for? 
And try not to lie to me.

704
01:07:00.808 --> 01:07:02.143
The book!

705
01:07:02.226 --> 01:07:05.396
The black book they found at 
Hamunaptra. He wants it back.

706
01:07:05.479 --> 01:07:07.648
He said to me it would be 
worth it's weight in gold.

707
01:07:07.732 --> 01:07:10.401
- What does he want the 
book for? - I don't know.

708
01:07:10.901 --> 01:07:14.321
Something about bringing his 
dead girlfriend back to life.

709
01:07:14.405 --> 01:07:16.824
But that's all. He just 
wants the book, I swear.

710
01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:20.327
Just the book, I swear. 
And your sister.

711
01:07:20.453 --> 01:07:21.620
But other than that...

712
01:08:12.630 --> 01:08:16.509
- That's two down, two to go. 
- Then he'll be coming after Evy.

713
01:08:16.675 --> 01:08:18.219
Guards in place!

714
01:08:18.302 --> 01:08:19.845
Reporting all clear, Sir!

715
01:08:19.929 --> 01:08:21.430
To hell with this?

716
01:08:21.514 --> 01:08:23.933
I'm going downstairs, get me 
a drink. You want something?

717
01:08:24.016 --> 01:08:27.228
- Yeah. Yeah, get me a glass 
of bourbon. - All right.

718
01:08:27.311 --> 01:08:29.605
- And a shot of bourbon. 
- Yeah, okay, okay.

719
01:08:29.688 --> 01:08:32.233
- And as bourbon chasser. 
- I'll get your damn bourbon!

720
01:08:32.316 --> 01:08:34.485
Don't worry about the door.

721
01:10:13.918 --> 01:10:15.920
Anck-Su-Namun.

722
01:10:26.847 --> 01:10:29.600
Hey, get your ugly 
face off of her!

723
01:10:33.145 --> 01:10:34.939
Look what I got.

724
01:10:51.789 --> 01:10:55.209
- You all right? 
- Well, I'm not sure.

725
01:11:05.511 --> 01:11:09.515
Well, according to legend, the black 
book the Americans found at Hamunaptra

726
01:11:09.598 --> 01:11:11.642
is supposed to bring 
people back from the dead.

727
01:11:11.725 --> 01:11:13.852
Until now, it was a notion I 
was unwilling to believe.

728
01:11:13.852 --> 01:11:16.397
Believe it, sister. That's what 
brought our buddy back to life?

729
01:11:16.480 --> 01:11:19.858
Yes. I'm thinking that if the black 
book can bring dead people to life...

730
01:11:19.942 --> 01:11:23.612
- Then maybe the gold book can 
kill him. - That's the myth.

731
01:11:23.696 --> 01:11:26.573
Now, we just have to find out 
where the gold book is hidden.

732
01:11:26.657 --> 01:11:28.284
Imhotep.

733
01:11:28.659 --> 01:11:30.244
Imhotep.

734
01:11:30.452 --> 01:11:32.162
Imhotep.

735
01:11:32.496 --> 01:11:34.248
Imhotep.

736
01:11:34.748 --> 01:11:36.542
Imhotep.

737
01:11:36.834 --> 01:11:40.921
Imhotep.

738
01:11:41.171 --> 01:11:47.094
Imhotep.

739
01:11:47.553 --> 01:11:49.346
Imhotep.

740
01:11:49.805 --> 01:11:51.015
Imhotep.

741
01:11:51.098 --> 01:11:55.102
Last but not least, my favorite 
plague, boils and sores.

742
01:11:55.185 --> 01:11:57.187
They have become his slaves.

743
01:11:57.563 --> 01:12:00.858
So it has begun, the 
beginning of the end.

744
01:12:00.941 --> 01:12:03.527
Not quite yet, it hasn't. 
Come on.

745
01:12:04.653 --> 01:12:06.363
Imhotep.

746
01:12:06.864 --> 01:12:08.699
Imhotep.

747
01:12:08.824 --> 01:12:10.367
Imhotep.

748
01:12:13.370 --> 01:12:16.915
Imhotep.

749
01:12:17.750 --> 01:12:19.376
Imhotep.

750
01:12:26.383 --> 01:12:29.219
According to Bembridge scholars, 
the Golden Book of Amun-Ra

751
01:12:29.303 --> 01:12:31.305
is located inside the 
statue of Anubis.

752
01:12:31.388 --> 01:12:33.390
- That's where we found the 
black book. - Exactly.

753
01:12:33.474 --> 01:12:35.351
Looks like the old boys at 
Bembridge were mistaken.

754
01:12:35.434 --> 01:12:37.061
They mixed the books up.

755
01:12:37.144 --> 01:12:38.937
Mixed up where they were buried.

756
01:12:39.021 --> 01:12:42.066
So, if the black book is 
inside the statue of Anubis,

757
01:12:42.149 --> 01:12:44.818
then the Golden book 
must be inside...

758
01:12:48.572 --> 01:12:51.992
- I think I'll go and get the 
car started. - I've got it.

759
01:12:52.076 --> 01:12:56.205
The Golden Book of Amun-Ra is at 
Hamunaptra inside the statue of Horus.

760
01:13:05.422 --> 01:13:07.591
Imhotep.

761
01:13:08.217 --> 01:13:10.803
Imhotep.

762
01:13:10.969 --> 01:13:15.682
Imhotep.

763
01:13:15.974 --> 01:13:18.102
Imhotep.

764
01:13:24.983 --> 01:13:27.444
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

765
01:13:29.196 --> 01:13:31.740
Get this thing in gear, boy. 
Let's get out of here.

766
01:13:31.824 --> 01:13:34.159
- Evy. Come on, Evy. Hurry up. 
- Imhotep!

767
01:13:34.326 --> 01:13:35.828
Imhotep!

768
01:13:42.459 --> 01:13:45.337
You're gonna get yours, Beni! 
You hear me?

769
01:13:45.921 --> 01:13:50.342
- You're gonna get yours! - Oh, 
like I've never heard that before!

770
01:14:20.706 --> 01:14:22.624
Hang on!

771
01:14:58.243 --> 01:15:00.954
Hey! O'Connell! O'Connell!

772
01:15:56.468 --> 01:15:57.636
Jump down!

773
01:16:00.639 --> 01:16:02.474
Move, move, move!

774
01:16:05.310 --> 01:16:07.020
Imhotep.

775
01:16:07.104 --> 01:16:08.689
Imhotep.

776
01:16:09.106 --> 01:16:10.649
Imhotep.

777
01:16:11.149 --> 01:16:16.321
Imhotep.

778
01:16:16.822 --> 01:16:18.615
Imhotep.

779
01:16:21.576 --> 01:16:23.328
It's the creature.

780
01:16:23.912 --> 01:16:25.747
He's fully regenerated.

781
01:16:31.128 --> 01:16:33.171
Come with me, my Princess.

782
01:16:33.338 --> 01:16:36.508
It is time to make 
you mine forever.

783
01:16:36.717 --> 01:16:39.011
For all eternity, idiot.

784
01:16:45.142 --> 01:16:48.478
Take my hand, and I will 
spare your friends.

785
01:16:49.688 --> 01:16:51.106
Oh, dear.

786
01:16:53.400 --> 01:16:56.111
- Have you got any bright ideas? 
- I'm thinking, I'm thinking.

787
01:16:56.194 --> 01:16:59.614
You better think of something fast, 
because if he turns me into a mummy,

788
01:16:59.698 --> 01:17:02.034
you're the first one 
I'm coming after.

789
01:17:06.038 --> 01:17:07.122
No.

790
01:17:07.205 --> 01:17:08.248
- Don't. 
- No!

791
01:17:08.332 --> 01:17:10.626
He has to take me to Hamunaptra 
to perform the ritual.

792
01:17:10.709 --> 01:17:14.338
She is right. Live 
today, fight tomorrow.

793
01:17:25.849 --> 01:17:28.560
I'll be seeing you again.

794
01:17:34.691 --> 01:17:36.026
Evelyn!

795
01:17:38.737 --> 01:17:41.907
- Hey, that's mine. 
- Thank you.

796
01:17:43.325 --> 01:17:44.576
Kill them all!

797
01:17:44.660 --> 01:17:46.870
No! Let go of me!

798
01:17:46.953 --> 01:17:48.538
- Imhotep. 
- Let go of me!

799
01:17:48.622 --> 01:17:51.583
- Goodbye, my friend. 
- Come here, you little...

800
01:17:51.666 --> 01:17:54.544
Imhotep.

801
01:17:54.920 --> 01:17:56.755
Imhotep.

802
01:18:00.550 --> 01:18:01.677
Come on!

803
01:18:01.760 --> 01:18:03.762
- What about my sister? 
- We're gonna get her back!

804
01:18:03.762 --> 01:18:05.472
Go!

805
01:18:05.555 --> 01:18:06.932
You're next!

806
01:18:08.433 --> 01:18:10.352
Come on! Give me your hand!

807
01:18:10.435 --> 01:18:12.604
- You go! 
- Come on!

808
01:18:12.688 --> 01:18:13.939
Go!

809
01:18:46.638 --> 01:18:49.641
Morning, Winston. A word?

810
01:18:51.143 --> 01:18:54.896
What's your little problem got to do 
with His Majesty's Royal Air Corps?

811
01:18:54.980 --> 01:18:56.523
Not a damn thing.

812
01:18:58.358 --> 01:19:00.902
- Is it dasngerous? - You 
probably won't live through it.

813
01:19:00.986 --> 01:19:02.904
By Jove, do you really think so?

814
01:19:02.988 --> 01:19:05.490
Everybody else we've bumped 
into has died. Why not you?

815
01:19:05.574 --> 01:19:08.243
What's the... What's 
the challenge, then?

816
01:19:08.326 --> 01:19:11.997
Rescue the damsel in distress, kill 
the bad guy, and save the world.

817
01:19:13.457 --> 01:19:15.917
Winston Havlock at 
your service, Sir.

818
01:19:27.179 --> 01:19:29.181
Are you all right?

819
01:19:30.056 --> 01:19:32.517
Do I bloody look all right?

820
01:19:36.563 --> 01:19:38.148
How you doing?

821
01:19:47.782 --> 01:19:51.411
See that? I've never 
seen one so big.

822
01:19:52.037 --> 01:19:53.955
- Never? 
- No!

823
01:20:06.760 --> 01:20:09.888
Get off me! Get off!

824
01:20:11.640 --> 01:20:13.517
I need a new job.

825
01:20:34.412 --> 01:20:35.956
Oh, my God.

826
01:20:36.414 --> 01:20:37.833
We're back.

827
01:20:50.345 --> 01:20:51.930
O'Connell.

828
01:21:04.484 --> 01:21:06.778
Oh, my God.

829
01:21:08.405 --> 01:21:12.367
Hey, Winston! Pedal faster!

830
01:21:14.578 --> 01:21:16.329
Hang on, men!

831
01:21:59.831 --> 01:22:02.042
Stop it! You'll kill them!

832
01:22:02.167 --> 01:22:03.835
That's the idea.

833
01:22:19.059 --> 01:22:21.436
Here I come, laddies!

834
01:22:48.838 --> 01:22:52.217
I love the whole sand-wall 
trick. It was beautiful.

835
01:22:52.300 --> 01:22:53.551
Bastard.

836
01:23:11.611 --> 01:23:13.571
Yeah, yeah. All right.

837
01:23:19.119 --> 01:23:21.705
Winston! Hey, Winston!

838
01:23:36.219 --> 01:23:39.764
Quicksand! Get back! 
It's quicksand?

839
01:24:53.379 --> 01:24:56.257
Bembridge scholars never 
wrote about this.

840
01:25:01.262 --> 01:25:03.681
Get off me. Get off!

841
01:25:49.602 --> 01:25:51.896
Wha... Wha...

842
01:26:12.834 --> 01:26:14.586
- Can you see... 
- Yeah.

843
01:26:14.669 --> 01:26:17.005
- Can you believe... 
- Yeah.

844
01:26:17.088 --> 01:26:18.840
- Can we just... 
- No.

845
01:26:29.684 --> 01:26:32.896
- Who the hell are these guys? 
- Priests.

846
01:26:33.354 --> 01:26:34.856
Imhotep's priests.

847
01:26:35.273 --> 01:26:36.816
All right, then.

848
01:27:24.739 --> 01:27:26.240
There he is!

849
01:27:27.408 --> 01:27:29.369
Hello, Horus, old boy.

850
01:27:38.586 --> 01:27:40.546
Time to close the door.

851
01:28:20.795 --> 01:28:22.505
Anck-Su-Namun.

852
01:28:31.639 --> 01:28:33.099
O'Connell!

853
01:28:33.850 --> 01:28:35.310
Jonathan!

854
01:28:46.154 --> 01:28:49.073
Damn. These guys just 
don't quit, do they?

855
01:28:49.198 --> 01:28:50.742
Keep digging.

856
01:29:14.557 --> 01:29:16.184
The Book of Amun-Ra.

857
01:29:24.609 --> 01:29:27.445
Save the girl. 
Kill the creature.

858
01:29:45.630 --> 01:29:47.548
You all right. Let's go.

859
01:30:42.603 --> 01:30:46.357
The Book of Amun-Ra! I 
found it, Evy! I found it!

860
01:30:48.151 --> 01:30:51.028
Shut up and get me 
off here, Jonathan!

861
01:30:51.362 --> 01:30:54.949
Open the book, Jonathan. It's 
the only way to kill him.

862
01:30:55.032 --> 01:30:57.827
You have to open the book 
and find the inscription.

863
01:30:57.910 --> 01:31:01.706
Well, I can't open it! 
It's locked or something.

864
01:31:03.458 --> 01:31:06.794
- We need the key, Evy! 
- It's inside his robes.

865
01:31:13.676 --> 01:31:14.927
O'Connell!

866
01:31:46.792 --> 01:31:48.169
Mummies.

867
01:31:59.639 --> 01:32:02.516
Look out! There's one there... 
O'Connell!

868
01:32:28.084 --> 01:32:30.169
Here's an inscription.

869
01:32:49.230 --> 01:32:50.856
Oh, boy.

870
01:32:57.822 --> 01:33:01.200
Oh, yeah. This just keeps 
getting better and better.

871
01:33:01.867 --> 01:33:04.036
- Do something, Jonathan. 
- Me?

872
01:33:04.120 --> 01:33:07.081
- You can command them. - You 
have got to be joking.

873
01:33:07.164 --> 01:33:10.668
Finish the inscription on the cover, 
idiot, then you can control them.

874
01:33:10.751 --> 01:33:12.587
Oh. Right.

875
01:33:50.249 --> 01:33:52.126
Hurry up, Jonathan!

876
01:34:23.991 --> 01:34:27.661
- I can't figure out this last 
symbol. - What does it look like?

877
01:34:41.759 --> 01:34:45.137
It's a bird. A stork!

878
01:34:58.025 --> 01:34:59.860
Ahmenophus.

879
01:35:01.570 --> 01:35:03.155
Oh, yes, I see.

880
01:35:49.034 --> 01:35:50.870
Anck-Su-Namun!

881
01:36:01.964 --> 01:36:03.549
Anck-Su-Namun!

882
01:36:31.118 --> 01:36:33.496
Evy, I've got it.

883
01:36:38.125 --> 01:36:39.627
Keep him busy.

884
01:36:43.464 --> 01:36:44.965
No problem.

885
01:36:57.353 --> 01:37:00.815
- Hurry, Evy! Hurry! 
- You're not helping.

886
01:37:09.865 --> 01:37:11.408
Oh! I've got it?

887
01:37:41.313 --> 01:37:44.483
I thought you said it 
was gonna kill him!

888
01:37:53.576 --> 01:37:55.035
He's mortal.

889
01:38:30.321 --> 01:38:33.407
Death is only the beginning.

890
01:39:03.562 --> 01:39:04.980
Time to go.

891
01:39:15.658 --> 01:39:18.494
You've lost the book! 
Jonathan, I can't believe...

892
01:39:18.577 --> 01:39:20.079
- Hurry! 
- Come on!

893
01:39:48.565 --> 01:39:51.360
- Couldn't we just... 
- No, Jonathan!

894
01:39:57.658 --> 01:39:59.159
O'Connell!

895
01:40:01.829 --> 01:40:05.040
- O'Connell! Wait! 
- Come on, come on!

896
01:40:05.290 --> 01:40:08.335
- Wait! Please! - Come 
on, come on! Beni!

897
01:40:10.170 --> 01:40:11.755
Goodbye, Beni.

898
01:40:14.883 --> 01:40:16.677
Look out, look out!

899
01:41:03.640 --> 01:41:06.101
Thank you. Thank you very much?

900
01:41:06.185 --> 01:41:10.022
You have earned the respect and 
gratitude of me and my people?

901
01:41:10.105 --> 01:41:12.816
Yes, well, it was nothing?

902
01:41:12.900 --> 01:41:15.194
May Allah smile upon you always.

903
01:41:17.237 --> 01:41:19.364
And yourself.

904
01:41:25.454 --> 01:41:28.248
- Yes, anytime. - Stay 
out of trouble.

905
01:41:29.333 --> 01:41:32.086
He's just leaving us here?

906
01:41:36.423 --> 01:41:40.219
Well, I guess we go home 
empty-handed again.

907
01:41:40.594 --> 01:41:42.387
I wouldn't say that.

908
01:41:44.598 --> 01:41:46.600
Oh, please!

909
01:41:55.734 --> 01:41:58.487
How about you, darling? Would 
you like a little kissy-wissy?

